; Storage regions (NVR 1.7). The compiler does not emit them yet, so this image is
; assembled by hand (generated, then kept as text); the graphs are the compiler's checked int64
; compare, increment and add. tests/backend/tier_programs_tests.cpp runs it in every tier, with
; the argument count selecting a trap case.
;
; F1, F2 print an int64, a uint64; F3 garbage(n): n texts nothing keeps, so collections run;
; F4, F5 add int64, uint64
; F6  nested regions per block                 prints 2, 1
; F7  a region per loop iteration              prints 300; the region is 51 cells at its largest
; F8, F9, F10 a fresh array and a holder with its cell move to the caller's region on return;
;     the callee's other array goes with its region       prints 5, 77
; F11 break and continue paths each release     prints 18
; F12, F13 a return leaves a region open        prints 150
; F14 the only reference to heap objects is held by region entries, across collections   prints 42, 43, 44
; F15 a region list grows in place and shrinks  prints 100, 99
; F16, F17 allocation into the caller's region by its token       prints 8
; F18 a hot loop that reads an array
; F19..F27 trap cases 1..9, by argument count: 1 read after release, 2 the same inside a hot loop
;     the tiers compile, 3 stack limit, 4 move to a region that does not enclose, 5 release twice,
;     6 a trap with nested regions open, 7 free of a region entry, 8 a token that never was one,
;     9 a heap handle moved to a region
nvr 1.7 profile 1
